async-profiler

  async --> asychronously collecting the stack trace sample and non blocking
  the overhead depends on the frequency, at 1Hz, the overhead is minimal
  
  overhead also depends on profiling type(mode):  cpu and memory
     cpu just stack trace, minimal
     memor mode, have to track memory alloc and dealloc, which is more resource intensive
  async-profiler is more suitable for cpu profiling, for memory, it can do with alloc event, but better analysis in conjunction with other tools

  async-profiler suffers JVM safepoint bias, that means the methods between safepoint won't be sampled
  JVM needs safepoint to suspend the execution of all threads to perform tasks that require a globally consistent view of the application's state
  safepoints are locations in the application's code where all threads are guaranteed to be in a safe and consistent state

    


linux perf does not suffer JVM safepoint bias,  but it can not get JVM related insights
